Author: matze4u <171579628+matze4u@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 27 21:14:44 2026 +0200

    fix(tests): stop the reach:doctor witness watching shared mutable state
    
    `git status --porcelain --ignored` over the whole worktree was the
    witness's run-window instrument for "reach:doctor mutates nothing". Any
    other parallel test writing into any gitignored scratch directory and
    removing it again (bench_ab_v2_run.test.ts against
    internal/bench/reports/ab-v2/, in this case) flipped a `!!` line into
    existence and back out during the witness's own window, producing a
    non-deterministic failure unrelated to the command under test.
    
    This is the second occurrence of the same shape (agents/runtime/ was
    the first, already removed from this witness). A pathspec-scoped
    porcelain call was considered and rejected: for a command whose only
    plausible write target is its own tracked surface, it reports nothing
    the tracked-file instrument does not already report, with less
    precision. The whole-worktree porcelain instrument is dropped instead,
    and the STRUCTURAL AST scan (already present) is promoted to the
    claim's primary carrier, backed by the tracked-file stats instrument.
    
    Adds a deterministic staged-interference test (writes and removes a
    file in the exact gitignored directory that tripped the original
    failure, from inside the witness's own run window) and a dedicated
    sensitivity test proving the STRUCTURAL scan fails a planted write and
    passes the same word in a comment, on an in-memory reach-shaped
    fixture.
    
    Flake-diagnosis: gitignored-dir-watch-scope | parallel writes to an
    unrelated ignored dir trip a whole-worktree witness

